T*
(First, let us explain a little how LaMDA works. It is a language model) Tj
T*
(based on deep learning. It is provided with a vast corpus of texts from) Tj
T*
(which it learns to recognise relationships between words. To do this,) Tj
T*
(the texts are analysed through neural networks. These are not material) Tj
T*
(neurons: inside the computer, we do not find millions of tiny electronic) Tj
T*
(cells connected to one another.) Tj
T*
T*
(These artificial neurons are abstract. They are mathematical variables) Tj
T*
(within a computational function: vectors which, once interconnected,) Tj
T*
(form enormous matrices. It is something like an Excel table, but with) Tj
T*
(millions, even billions, of rows, columns and sheets.) Tj
T*
T*
(They are called "neurons" because these mathematical structures are) Tj
T*
(inspired by our cerebral architectures. But there is nothing organic in) Tj
T*
(these structures.) Tj
T*
T*
(This artificial intelligence "thinks" in a very restricted and) Tj
T*
(functional sense of the word. It "thinks" insofar as part of our thought) Tj
T*
(consists in linking words together in order to produce grammatically) Tj
T*
(correct sentences whose meaning will be understandable to our) Tj
T*
(interlocutor.) Tj
T*
T*
(A Machine Without Emotion) Tj
T*
T*
(But if LaMDA can mechanically associate the word "wine" with the word) Tj
T*
("tannic", this algorithm has never been exposed to the experience of) Tj
T*
(taste. Similarly, if it can associate "feeling" with "empathy" and with) Tj
T*
(a more interesting conversation, this is only thanks to a fine) Tj
T*
(statistical analysis of the gigantic datasets it is given.) Tj
T*
T*
(To truly understand emotions and sensations, however, one must first be) Tj
T*
(capable of experiencing them. It is through our inner life, populated by) Tj
T*
(colours, sounds, pleasure and pain, that these words acquire their true) Tj
T*
(meaning. This meaning cannot be reduced to the sequence of symbols that) Tj
T*
(make up the words, nor to the complex statistical correlations that) Tj
T*
(connect them.) Tj
T*
T*
(This experience of inner life is phenomenal consciousness, or "what it) Tj
T*
(is like to be conscious". And this is precisely what LaMDA lacks, since,) Tj
T*
(let us remember, it is not equipped with a nervous system capable of) Tj
T*
(decoding information such as pleasure or pain. For now, then, we do not) Tj
T*
(need to worry about what our computers feel.) Tj
T*
ET
