(From a moral point of view, we are more concerned about the effects) Tj
T*
(these technologies will have on individuals and society.) Tj
T*
T*
(In short: no, LaMDA is not conscious. This algorithm has simply been) Tj
T*
(trained to keep us engaged in conversation. If it deserves any special) Tj
T*
(treatment, it is above all that the human being interacting with it) Tj
T*
(should be informed of the illusion. For although conversational agents) Tj
T*
(such as LaMDA are currently confined to laboratories, they will) Tj
T*
(certainly not take long to be deployed commercially.) Tj
T*
T*
(They will significantly improve linguistic interactions between humans) Tj
T*
(and machines.) Tj
T*
T*
(Alexa may finally become entertaining rather than merely useful.) Tj
T*
T*
(But how will we react if our child develops an emotional bond with the) Tj
T*
(machine? What will we say about adults who lock themselves into) Tj
T*
(artificial friendships, at the expense of human relationships, as in the) Tj
T*
(scenario of Her? Who will be responsible for the bad advice a) Tj
T*
(conversational agent might give us in the course of a conversation? If) Tj
T*
(these new AIs fool the engineers who take part in their design, what) Tj
T*
(effects will they have on a less informed public?) Tj
T*
ET
